{
  "category": "Wrestling Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It overwhelms opponents with quick moves, but sometimes it showboats for too long when it’s using a special move and gets itself into a pinch.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "In combat, Hawlucha leaps nimbly about, taking advantage of its opponents’ blind spots. It’s also skilled at using superb submission holds.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It drives its opponents to exhaustion with its agile maneuvers, then ends the fight with a flashy finishing move.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It always strikes a pose before going for its finishing move. Sometimes opponents take advantage of that time to counterattack.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
